WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.700
In 1980, Stephen King published one of his
most disturbing stories, a novella called

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.320
The Mist.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.800
The story got even more disturbing when filmmaker
Frank Darabont wrote a new ending for his

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.460
2007 movie adaptation.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.300
The film's final twist devastated audiences,
and it still traumatizes people today.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.320
Here's what it all means.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.180
So considering this movie's over ten years
old, let's do a quick recap so we're all on

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:25.800
the same page.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.960
The Mist tells the story of a dad named David
and his son, Billy, who get caught inside

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
a supermarket when a mysterious and dangerous
mist engulfs his small town in Maine.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.080
Over the course of the film, we learn a few
things: the mist is full of horrors, which

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.560
include deadly tentacles and giant wasps and
pterodactyls.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.080
We also learn that one of the store's patrons,
Amanda Dumfries, carries a gun.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:52.680
But before we skip to the end, there's one
important moment that we need to touch on:

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.360
Before all the monsters show up, but after
the parking lot has filled with fog, everybody

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.260
agrees to stay inside…except for one unnamed
woman, played by Melissa McBride.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.710
She's a mom who left her kids at home to do
some quick grocery shopping, but with the

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.560
world falling apart, she can't sit around
twiddling her thumbs.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.500
She's got to get back to her kids.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.670
Several people try to stop her, but she won't
hear it.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.000
And when she asks for help, everybody goes
quiet.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.900
Teary-eyed and disgusted, she curses the group...

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.480
"I hope you all rot in hell."

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.700
...and she strides into the mist, having faith
she can get home in one piece.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.860
It's a nerve-wracking and heartbreaking moment…and
one we'll need to file away for future reference.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.120
This moment comes around full circle and hammers
some themes down hard.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:43.560
Eventually, after the mist starts belching
up monsters, tentacles, and tons of baby spiders,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.740
neighborhood nutjob Mrs. Carmody, a bloodthirsty
Bible-thumper who thinks the end times are

00:01:48.749 --> 00:01:53.139
nigh, starts gathering followers who oppose
our hero David and his allies' attempts to

00:01:53.139 --> 00:01:55.340
stay smart and survive during the crisis.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.600
Suffice it to say: this whole mist thing is
pretty bad news, guys.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.460
Eventually, the survivors inside the supermarket
begin to turn on each other, Lord of the Flies

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.000
style.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.460
A small group of allies join David and Billy
as they escape from the store in the hopes

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.400
that whatever's lurking in the mist isn't
as bad as the horror of human beings at their

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:12.940
worst.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:17.920
Several of them are picked off by killer bugs,
but the surviving members, David, Billy, and

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.040
three others named Amanda, Dan, and Irene,
pile into a car and drive into the fog…

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:26.000
but not before David grabs Amanda's gun.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.610
As they drive down the road, they see toppled
telephone poles, wrecked cars, and a school

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.050
bus savaged by spiders.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:38.239
They find the webbed-up body of David's dead
wife, watch an enormous Lovecraftian creature

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:42.459
lumber by, and no matter how far they drive,
the mist stretches on forever.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:46.360
Eventually, they run out of gas, and as they
hear the monsters outside, they make a decision:

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.600
a bullet is better than a bug.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.660
David checks the gun, sees there are only
four bullets for five people, and does the

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:54.660
deed.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.640
He kills everyone in the car, including his
son.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.180
David is the only one left alive, howling
like a wounded animal.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.820
"AHHHHHHHHHH!"

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:10.120
Then, he starts begging for the monsters to
finish him off.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.500
"C'mon!

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.340
C'mon!"

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.860
But his despair deepens when seconds later,
a military convoy rumbles out of the mist.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.720
Adding insult to injury, David sees vehicles
full of survivors, including Melissa McBride

00:03:29.731 --> 00:03:30.750
and her kids.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.260
The mist clears, and David is left screaming
in pain.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.920
If only he'd waited a few more seconds, his
son would still be alive.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.660
"AHHHHH!"

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.220
And on that cheery note, the film fades to
black.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.560
"That's all folks!"

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:53.980
If you couldn't tell by the end of the film,
The Mist doesn't think very highly of mankind.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.780
It shares a worldview with movies like Night
of the Living Dead and John Carpenter's The

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.820
Thing.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:03.140
According to The Mist, people are prone to
paranoia and distrust, and will turn on each

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:04.820
other when things go south.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:09.240
But at the same time, the movie is ultimately
a message about the power of hope, and what

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.400
happens when hope disappears.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:13.060
Speaking with Yahoo!

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:17.320
Entertainment, Frank Darabont explained The
Mist works as a companion piece with his first

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.680
feature, The Shawshank Redemption:

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.440
"If Shawshank is the movie about the value
of hope, then The Mist becomes a movie about

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:25.320
the danger of hopelessness."

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:30.420
So in the '94 classic, Andy Dufresne hangs
onto hope and escapes from prison.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.680
"I guess it comes down to a simple choice,
really.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.200
Get busy living.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.960
Or get busy dying."

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.360
But in The Mist, instead of getting busy living,
David and his companions do the other one.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.620
While Andy keeps the faith and finds freedom,
David gives up and loses everything when salvation

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:50.460
was so close.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.800
And this is where Melissa McBride's character
comes back in.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.560
This mom marched into the fog to rescue her
kids, even though everyone else was scared

00:04:58.600 --> 00:04:59.140
and tried to stop her.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.380
She never let go of hope, and as a result,
she saved her children.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:07.440
David, on the other hand, fell into despair
and lost his son's life.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.980
So what's the big moral of The Mist?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:14.580
Even if life feels like a never-ending nightmare,
be like that mom, because you never know when

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.760
the mist will fade away.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:20.300
Both the novella and movie versions of The
Mist are excellent, but they radically differ

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.300
when it comes to the ending.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.230
While the film goes in a decidedly dark direction,
King's novella is much more ambiguous.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:30.770
In fact, the author actually leaves his readers
with some hope that things will work out for

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:31.300
David and his crew.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.060
Team David escapes the supermarket, but instead
of committing mass suicide, David turns on

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.080
the radio and thinks he hears a voice say
the word "Hartford."

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.520
Encouraged, he believes Hartford, Connecticut,
might be a safe zone, and he heads in that

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.080
direction.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.200
The novella ends with David narrating these
final lines:

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.440
"I'm going to bed now.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:53.320
But first I'm going to kiss my son and whisper
two words in his ear…Two words that sound

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:53.840
a bit alike.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.480
One of them is Hartford.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:56.960
The other is hope."

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.800
And that's where the book ends, hinting that
maybe Team David is going to be okay.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:05.520
Obviously, Darabont decided to traumatize
moviegoers, but Stephen King was totally okay

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.140
with the movie's new ending.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:12.020
When Darabont asked for King's opinion on
the nihilistic finale, the author gave him

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.140
two thumbs up.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:18.860
King even famously declared that, quote, "anybody
who reveals the last 5 minutes of this film

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.120
should be hung from their neck until dead."

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.560
"Okay, uh…"

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.200
We really hope he doesn't watch this video.

